@startuml check_in_sequence
title Detailed Sequence Diagram — Check In

actor Employee
participant "Attendance Page\n(React)" as UI
participant "PointageController" as Controller
participant "PointageService" as Service
participant "PointageRepository" as Repo
participant "AttendanceNotification\n(Event)" as Event
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Employee -> UI : Open attendance page
UI -> Controller : GET /api/pointages/today
Controller -> Service : getTodayPointage(userId)
Service -> Repo : getTodayPointage(userId)
Repo -> DB : SELECT pointage for today
DB --> Repo : record or null
Repo --> Service : pointage
Service --> Controller : today status
Controller --> UI : JSON response
UI --> Employee : Display history and check-in button

Employee -> UI : Click Check In
UI -> Controller : POST /api/pointages/entree
Controller -> Service : pointerEntree(userId)

Service -> Repo : getTodayPointage(userId)

alt Already checked in today
  Repo --> Service : existing heure_entree
  Service --> Controller : ValidationException
  Controller --> UI : 422 error
  UI --> Employee : Display error message
else First check-in of the day
  Service -> Repo : pointer(userId, 'entree')
  Repo -> DB : INSERT/UPDATE pointage\n(heure_entree, date)
  DB --> Repo : saved record
  Repo --> Service : Pointage

  Service -> Service : Detect late check-in\n(after 09:15)
  Service -> Event : dispatch(AttendanceNotification)
  Event --> Service : notification sent

  Service --> Controller : Pointage
  Controller --> UI : 200 OK + pointage
  UI --> Employee : Update UI (checked in)
end

@enduml
